GWT Material Widgets is an independent TeaVM port of GWT Material Design.
Original widget, jQuery/JSCore, selected addins and showcase code is the work of GwtMaterialDesign
and its contributors, distributed under Apache License 2.0. Original notices are
retained in the pinned source archives and derived artifacts.

The io.instanto groupId identifies this independent distribution and avoids
confusion with upstream releases. Original Java package names are preserved.

Materialize, jQuery and fonts retain their own licenses in the archived sources.
See upstream/assessment-lock.json for repository URLs and exact revisions.

The showcase shell is derived from gmd-core-demo's ApplicationView.ui.xml and
app.css. Retained views and UiBinder templates are tracked by the generated
showcase-inputs.sha256 manifest. See docs/DESIGN.md for the construction-shell,
font-source and animation-image adaptations.

The selected addins include original WebP, autocomplete, combo-box, input-mask
and time-picker code and resources. Combo-box native values and the selected
dark-theme registry, plus clock pointer activation, are adapted as described in
docs/DESIGN.md.
Date-picker pointer activation, popup disposal and native Date property access
are adapted as described in docs/DESIGN.md.
Material tab initialisation and indicator cleanup are adapted to avoid stale
animation targets during reload. See docs/DESIGN.md for the exact boundary.

Media images are local copies of the original GWT Material demo assets.
The video iframe substitutes an original silent sample. Material slider and
lightbox lifecycle resources are adapted for disposal.
See docs/MEDIA-ASSETS.md and docs/DESIGN.md for provenance and changes.

Table widgets come from GwtMaterialDesign/gwt-material-table; the corrected
source used here is committed as upstream/gwt-material-table.zip. The six table
showcase views, UiBinder templates, descriptions, data generators and asynchronous
fixture service come from GwtMaterialDesign/gmd-table-demo, under Apache 2.0.
Their source revisions are recorded in upstream/assessment-lock.json. The table
demo bundles Faker.js; its original resource is retained and its MIT notice is
included under licenses/faker-MIT.txt in the showcase.
The fixture avatar is an original Instanto SVG, embedded in the generated examples.
See docs/TABLE-DESIGN.md for the table adaptations and shared compatibility changes.

The 18 full-page navigation views and templates come from
GwtMaterialDesign/gwt-material-patterns, under Apache 2.0. Their construction
boundary, local links and decorative image substitutions are described in
docs/DESIGN.md. Side Profile is original GWT Material Addins code.
